-- ako/mxcli#1514 (upstream mendixlabs/mxcli#1604): an @expect written over two
-- lines kept only its first, with no message. When the first line was a
-- complete expression the test ran a different assertion from the one written:
-- with `and` it could pass on less, with `or` it could fail although the whole
-- assertion held. An @expect (and an @verify) now runs on, as a javadoc tag's
-- text does, to the next @tag or the end of the comment.
--
-- Setup: test-runner-1514-setup.mdl. Then:
--
--   mxcli test mdl-examples/bug-tests/test-runner-1514-multiline-expect.test.mdl --list
--
-- lists the whole assertion for each test (before the fix: only the first line,
-- and an "expected a value at column 16" ERROR for test_3), and
--
--   mxcli test mdl-examples/bug-tests/test-runner-1514-multiline-expect.test.mdl -p app.mpr --local
--
-- reports test_1 FAIL ("expected $r = 'a;b' and length($r) = 4") and test_2 and
-- test_3 PASS. Before the fix test_1 PASSED — it asserted only $r = 'a;b' — and
-- test_2 FAILED with "expected $r = 'zzz', actual: a;b". Measured on 11.13.0.
--
-- `make check-mdl` sweeps this file without a project: test_3 is the shape that
-- did not compile before, so the sweep fails if the continuation is lost again.
-- The negative twin is test-runner-1514-text-after-expect.fail.test.mdl.
mdl 1;
/**
 * @test and on the next line: the whole assertion is false
 * @expect $r = 'a;b'
 *   and length($r) = 4
 */
$r = call microflow Probe.SUB_Make();
/

/**
 * @test or on the next line: the whole assertion is true
 * @expect $r = 'zzz'
 *   or $r = 'a;b'
 */
$r = call microflow Probe.SUB_Make();
/

/**
 * @test open parenthesis on the first line
 * @expect ($r = 'a;b' and
 *   length($r) = 3)
 */
$r = call microflow Probe.SUB_Make();
/
